      "en": "I do not think I am deceiving myself when I say that though I did not realise this in the beginning, my researches have bearing on all the conditions that permit us to maintain thought in the state of ‘openness’, in contradistinction to a systematised dogmatics closed in on itself. It is in this sense, it seems to me, and in this spirit, that the reader should approach this difficult and, in places, disconcerting book that is now presented to the English speaking public. — Autumn, 1950 GaBRIEL MarceEn XIII % = ; » i 7\" . ‘ oa a > ‘ ‘ s ‘ = } ~~ ~ ~ = > a . = . —— = i <——e ~ 7 . ] cant = 4 i \" iT = i ‘ i we = ¥ Py 7 é 1 iaaliiene! tat Sy eS ’ : 24 Si ‘ — oft, Se ae ¥ : a , a \" Pr: \\ ns oy ¢ i“ ~ Me ie ’ as Hi » Sn : 1 ial Ei rs 4. > : 4 pe . - ~~ ie <a i j : ‘ P ™ ‘ig j 7i y ab J ei aS Re ¥ ‘i ~ t 1@ COONTISELNeLiS Translator’s Note page v AUTHOR’S PREFACE to the English Edition page vii page 1 PART tf page 129 Page 32) INDEX page 341 METAPHYSICAL JOURNAL"
